# Accepted risks for a zero-cost deployment. Each entry has a reason; revisit
# if the project gets a budget (see docs/adr/0004-zero-cost-security-tradeoffs.md).

# CloudFront without WAF: AWS WAF costs at least $5/month + per-request fees.
# Abuse is bounded by API throttling, the endpoint cap and the static, read-only site.
AVD-AWS-0011

# CloudFront minimum TLS version: the default *.cloudfront.net certificate fixes the
# policy; a custom domain + ACM certificate is out of scope.
AVD-AWS-0013

# Customer-managed KMS keys (S3, SNS, SQS, DynamoDB, logs) cost $1/key/month.
# Everything is encrypted at rest with AWS-owned/managed keys instead.
AVD-AWS-0132
AVD-AWS-0136
AVD-AWS-0135

# SNS topic not encrypted: CloudWatch alarms cannot publish to a topic encrypted with
# the AWS-managed aws/sns key, and a customer key costs money. Alerts carry no secrets.
AVD-AWS-0095

# Bootstrap deploy role uses service-level wildcards (dynamodb:*, lambda:*, ...) because
# Terraform must create/update/delete those resources. IAM itself is limited to
# roles named vigilwatch-*, and the role is only assumable from main/production via OIDC.
AVD-AWS-0057
